Construction Management Platform

**API & INTEGRATION SPEC SHEET**

*Document 5 of 9 \| Version 1.0 \| Confidential*

March 2026

FOR ENGINEERING --- CONFIDENTIAL

**Table of Contents**

**1. Overview & API Standards**

This document specifies every API endpoint, request/response format,
authentication pattern, and third-party integration for \[PLATFORM
NAME\] v1.0. It serves as the primary reference for frontend engineers,
mobile engineers, and any third-party integration developers.

**1.1 API Design Standards**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Standard**       **Specification**
  ------------------ ----------------------------------------------------
  API Style          RESTful JSON API --- consistent resource-based URL
                     structure

  Base URL           https://api.platformname.com/v1

  Authentication     JWT Bearer token --- Authorization: Bearer \<token\>
                     header on all protected routes

  Content Type       application/json for all requests and responses

  Versioning         URL-based versioning --- /v1/ prefix. Breaking
                     changes increment to /v2/

  Date Format        ISO 8601 --- all dates as TIMESTAMPTZ:
                     2026-03-15T14:30:00Z

  Monetary Values    All amounts in cents (integer) --- never floating
                     point. \$1,500.00 = 150000

  IDs                UUID v4 strings --- never expose integer IDs in API
                     responses

  Pagination         Cursor-based pagination ---
                     ?cursor=\<uuid\>&limit=\<n\> (max 100 per page)

  Sorting            ?sort=created_at&order=desc --- field name and
                     direction

  Filtering          ?status=active&project_id=\<uuid\> --- query param
                     filters per resource

  Error Format       Consistent JSON error envelope (see Section 1.3)

  Rate Limiting      Per-tenant limits returned in X-RateLimit-Limit,
                     X-RateLimit-Remaining headers

  CORS               Strict origin allowlisting --- no wildcard. Web app
                     domain + mobile deep link schemes
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**1.2 Standard Response Envelope**

> // Success --- single resource
>
> {
>
> \"data\": { \"id\": \"uuid\", \"name\": \"Main St Office\", \... },
>
> \"meta\": { \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-15T14:30:00Z\" }
>
> }
>
> // Success --- collection
>
> {
>
> \"data\": \[ { \"id\": \"uuid\", \... }, \... \],
>
> \"meta\": {
>
> \"total\": 142,
>
> \"cursor\": \"uuid-of-last-item\",
>
> \"has_more\": true,
>
> \"timestamp\": \"2026-03-15T14:30:00Z\"
>
> }
>
> }

**1.3 Error Response Format**

> {
>
> \"error\": {
>
> \"code\": \"RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND\", // Machine-readable code
>
> \"message\": \"Project not found\", // Human-readable message
>
> \"field\": \"project_id\", // Field that caused error (validation
> only)
>
> \"request_id\": \"req_abc123\" // For support log correlation
>
> }
>
> }

**1.4 Standard HTTP Status Codes**

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Code**        **Meaning**     **When Used**
  --------------- --------------- ----------------------------------------------
  200 OK          Success         GET, PUT, PATCH --- resource returned or
                                  updated

  201 Created     Resource        POST --- new resource created, returns created
                  created         resource

  204 No Content  Success, no     DELETE --- resource deleted
                  body            

  400 Bad Request Validation      Invalid input, missing required fields
                  error           

  401             Auth required   Missing or invalid JWT token
  Unauthorized                    

  403 Forbidden   Permission      Valid token but insufficient role/permission
                  denied          

  404 Not Found   Resource        Resource does not exist or belongs to
                  missing         different tenant

  409 Conflict    State conflict  Duplicate unique value, invalid state
                                  transition

  422             Business logic  Valid format but violates business rules
  Unprocessable   error           

  429 Too Many    Rate limited    Per-tenant rate limit exceeded
  Requests                        

  500 Internal    Server error    Unexpected server-side error --- logged and
  Error                           alerted
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**2. Authentication Endpoints**

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Method**   **Endpoint**             **Auth**   **Description**
  ------------ ------------------------ ---------- ---------------------------------
  **POST**     /auth/signup             None       Create new tenant and admin user.
                                                   Triggers: tenant provisioning,
                                                   Stripe customer creation, welcome
                                                   email

  **POST**     /auth/login              None       Authenticate user --- returns
                                                   access_token (JWT) and sets
                                                   refresh_token httpOnly cookie

  **POST**     /auth/refresh            Cookie     Exchange refresh token for new
                                                   access token --- silent token
                                                   renewal

  **POST**     /auth/logout             JWT        Revoke current session --- adds
                                                   jti to Redis blacklist

  **POST**     /auth/forgot-password    None       Send password reset email with
                                                   secure time-limited token

  **POST**     /auth/reset-password     None       Reset password using token from
                                                   email

  **POST**     /auth/verify-email       None       Verify email address using token
                                                   from signup email

  **POST**     /auth/mfa/setup          JWT        Generate TOTP secret and QR code
                                                   for MFA setup

  **POST**     /auth/mfa/verify         JWT        Verify TOTP code to activate MFA
                                                   on user account

  **POST**     /auth/mfa/challenge      None       Submit TOTP code during login
                                                   when MFA is enabled
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**2.1 POST /auth/signup --- Request Body**

> {
>
> \"company_name\": \"ABC General Contractors\",
>
> \"trade_type\": \"gc\",
>
> \"first_name\": \"John\",
>
> \"last_name\": \"Smith\",
>
> \"email\": \"john@abcgc.com\",
>
> \"password\": \"SecurePass123!\",
>
> \"subscription_tier\": \"professional\",
>
> \"billing_cycle\": \"monthly\",
>
> \"stripe_payment_method_id\": \"pm_stripe_id\" // from Stripe.js
>
> }

**2.2 POST /auth/login --- Response**

> {
>
> \"data\": {
>
> \"access_token\": \"eyJhbGci\...\",
>
> \"expires_in\": 86400,
>
> \"user\": { \"id\": \"uuid\", \"email\": \"\...\", \"role\":
> \"owner\", \"tenant_id\": \"t_001\" },
>
> \"tenant\": { \"id\": \"t_001\", \"name\": \"ABC General
> Contractors\", \"tier\": \"professional\" }
>
> }
>
> }

**3. Tenant & User Management Endpoints**

**3.1 Tenant**

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Method**   **Endpoint**                   **Auth**   **Description**
  ------------ ------------------------------ ---------- ---------------------------------
  **GET**      /tenant                        JWT        Get current tenant profile,
                                                         settings, subscription details

  **PUT**      /tenant                        JWT        Update tenant profile --- name,
                                                         branding, default settings

  **GET**      /tenant/subscription           JWT        Get full subscription details,
                                                         add-ons, billing history

  **POST**     /tenant/subscription/upgrade   JWT        Upgrade tier or add modules ---
                                                         triggers Stripe proration

  **DELETE**   /tenant                        JWT        Initiate tenant cancellation ---
                                                         starts 30-day retention window.
                                                         Owner only.
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**3.2 Users**

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Method**   **Endpoint**             **Auth**   **Description**
  ------------ ------------------------ ---------- ---------------------------------
  **GET**      /users                   JWT        List all users for tenant ---
                                                   paginated. Supports ?role= filter

  **GET**      /users/:id               JWT        Get single user profile

  **POST**     /users/invite            JWT        Send user invitation email ---
                                                   creates pending invitation record

  **PUT**      /users/:id               JWT        Update user profile, role, or
                                                   notification preferences

  **DELETE**   /users/:id               JWT        Deactivate user --- soft delete,
                                                   data preserved. Admin only.

  **GET**      /users/invitations       JWT        List pending invitations

  **DELETE**   /users/invitations/:id   JWT        Revoke pending invitation

  **POST**     /users/accept-invite     None       Accept invitation --- creates
                                                   user account linked to tenant
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------

