**12. Mobile-Specific Endpoints**

The following endpoints are designed specifically for mobile use cases
--- optimized for low-bandwidth conditions and offline sync
requirements.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Method**   **Endpoint**                        **Auth**   **Description**
  ------------ ----------------------------------- ---------- ---------------------------------
  **GET**      /mobile/sync                        JWT        Full sync payload for offline use
                                                              --- returns all active project
                                                              data, tasks, and plans metadata
                                                              since last_sync_at timestamp

  **POST**     /mobile/sync/push                   JWT        Push offline-created records to
                                                              server --- batch upload of time
                                                              entries, field reports, task
                                                              completions, photos created while
                                                              offline

  **GET**      /mobile/projects/:id/plan-urls      JWT        Pre-signed download URLs for all
                                                              current plan revisions --- for
                                                              offline caching

  **POST**     /mobile/photos/batch-upload-url     JWT        Get batch pre-signed URLs for
                                                              multiple photos --- mobile
                                                              uploads directly to S3

  **POST**     /mobile/daily-reports/voice-draft   JWT        Accept voice transcription text
                                                              --- returns formatted daily
                                                              report draft for user review

  **GET**      /mobile/schedule/today              JWT        Today\'s tasks for current user
                                                              --- optimized single-call
                                                              response for morning field
                                                              check-in

  **POST**     /mobile/device-token                JWT        Register device push notification
                                                              token --- APNs (iOS) or FCM
                                                              (Android)

  **DELETE**   /mobile/device-token                JWT        Unregister device token on logout
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**12.1 Offline Sync Architecture**

The mobile app operates in offline-first mode. When connectivity is
lost, all writes are queued locally in SQLite on the device. When
connectivity is restored, the sync engine runs:

-   Step 1: POST /mobile/sync/push --- push all queued local writes to
    the server in a single batch

-   Step 2: Server processes writes in order --- returns
    success/conflict status per record

-   Step 3: GET /mobile/sync --- pull any server-side changes since last
    sync timestamp

-   Step 4: Apply server changes to local SQLite, resolve any conflicts
    using last-write-wins per record

-   Step 5: Update last_sync_at timestamp --- stored locally and sent
    with every sync request

> **Conflict Resolution Rule:**
>
> For field data (time entries, task completions, daily reports) the
> server timestamp wins on conflict --- the server is the authoritative
> record. The app surfaces a conflict notification to the user when a
> local record was overwritten by a server update during sync.

**13. QuickBooks Online Integration**

QuickBooks Online (QBO) is the highest-priority integration in v1.0. It
is a bi-directional sync --- data flows both from QBO into the platform
and from the platform into QBO. The integration uses the Intuit QBO REST
API (OAuth 2.0).

**13.1 OAuth 2.0 Connection Flow**

-   Step 1: Tenant clicks \'Connect QuickBooks\' in Settings

-   Step 2: Platform redirects to Intuit OAuth 2.0 authorization page

-   Step 3: Tenant logs into QuickBooks and grants permission

-   Step 4: Intuit redirects back to platform with authorization code

-   Step 5: Platform exchanges code for access_token + refresh_token

-   Step 6: Platform stores encrypted tokens in tenant settings JSONB
    --- realm_id (company ID) stored for all future API calls

-   Step 7: Initial sync triggered --- imports chart of accounts,
    customers, vendors

**13.2 Bi-Directional Sync Mapping**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Platform     **Direction**   **QBO Entity** **Sync          **Notes**
  Entity**                                      Trigger**       
  -------------- --------------- -------------- --------------- ---------------------------
  Client         Platform → QBO  Customer       On client       Creates/updates QBO
                                                create/update   Customer. Sub-customer
                                                                hierarchy for project-level
                                                                P&L.

  Vendor         Platform → QBO  Vendor         On vendor       Syncs vendor name, contact,
                                                create/update   payment terms.

  Project        Platform → QBO  Sub-Customer   On project      QBO sub-customer under
                                                create          parent client. Enables
                                                                per-project P&L reporting
                                                                in QBO.

  Invoice        Platform → QBO  Invoice        On invoice      Creates QBO invoice against
  (owner)                                       approval        customer. Line items map to
                                                                service items.

  Invoice (sub)  QBO → Platform  Bill           On QBO bill     Sub bills entered in QBO
                                                creation        sync back as sub invoice
                                                                records in platform.

  Payment        QBO → Platform  Payment        On QBO payment  Updates platform invoice
  received                                      post            status to \'paid\' with
                                                                payment date.

  Chart of       QBO → Platform  Account        On initial      Populates budget category
  Accounts                                      connect + daily and cost code options in
                                                sync            platform.

  Time entries   Platform → QBO  Time Activity  On payroll run  Exports labor hours by
                                                trigger         employee and job for QBO
                                                                Payroll or export.

  Change order   Platform → QBO  Invoice line   On CO approval  Adds CO value to project
  amount                         item                           invoice in QBO.

  Expense/bill   QBO → Platform  Bill           On QBO bill     Syncs vendor bills to
                                                creation        platform budget actuals by
                                                                cost category.
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**13.3 Sync Engine Design**

-   Sync runs on a background job queue --- not on-demand API calls (too
    slow for UX)

-   Incremental sync every 15 minutes --- fetches only records modified
    since last sync timestamp

-   Full sync available on demand from Settings --- for initial setup or
    after resolving conflicts

-   Sync errors logged to a sync_log table --- visible to tenant admin
    in Settings \> QuickBooks

-   Conflict handling: platform changes take precedence for project/job
    data; QBO takes precedence for accounting/payment data

-   Webhook listener for real-time QBO events --- payments, bill
    approvals, account changes

**13.4 QBO API Endpoints Used**

  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **QBO Endpoint**                     **Method**   **Purpose**
  ------------------------------------ ------------ ------------------------------------
  /v3/company/{realmId}/customer       POST/PUT     Create and update customers and
                                                    sub-customers

  /v3/company/{realmId}/vendor         POST/PUT     Create and update vendors

  /v3/company/{realmId}/invoice        POST/PUT     Create and update invoices

  /v3/company/{realmId}/bill           GET          Retrieve vendor bills for expense
                                                    sync

  /v3/company/{realmId}/payment        GET          Retrieve customer payments

  /v3/company/{realmId}/account        GET          Chart of accounts for budget mapping

  /v3/company/{realmId}/timeactivity   POST         Post time entries for payroll

  /v3/company/{realmId}/query          GET          FIQL query for incremental sync ---
                                                    ?query=SELECT \* FROM Invoice WHERE
                                                    MetaData.LastUpdatedTime \> \'\...\'
  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

