**14.4 Weather API (OpenWeatherMap)**

Used to auto-populate weather conditions on daily field reports. Called
when a daily report is created with a GPS location.

> GET https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather
>
> ?lat={gps_lat}&lon={gps_lng}&appid={API_KEY}&units=imperial

Response mapped to daily_reports.weather_conditions JSONB: temperature
(F), condition description, wind speed (mph), precipitation (in). If the
GPS location is unavailable, weather field is left null --- not required
for report submission.

**14.5 Google Maps / Apple Maps**

-   Address validation: Google Places Autocomplete API on all address
    input fields --- standardizes address format

-   Geocoding: Google Geocoding API converts validated address to
    lat/lng for site_address.lat and site_address.lng

-   Geofencing: Platform computes distance between clock-in GPS and
    project site coordinates --- alert if \> 500 feet

-   Navigation: Deep-link to native Maps app from project detail ---
    google.maps:// or maps:// scheme on mobile

