**16. Localization API Standards**

Every API endpoint supports localization through a combination of the
Accept-Language request header and the user\'s stored preferred_language
preference. The API is locale-aware without requiring locale-specific
endpoint variants.

**16.1 Locale Resolution on Every Request**

> Locale resolution order (highest to lowest priority):
>
> 1\. users.preferred_language (from JWT claims)
>
> 2\. Accept-Language header on the request
>
> 3\. tenants.default_language (from JWT claims)
>
> 4\. \'en\' fallback

**16.2 Locale-Affected API Behaviors**

  -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  **API Behavior**      **Locale Effect**
  --------------------- -------------------------------------------------
  Error response        The data.error.message field is returned in the
  messages              resolved locale. The error.code is always English
                        --- machine-readable codes never change.

  Notification dispatch When an API action triggers a notification (e.g.
                        inspection recorded → notify PM), the
                        notification service resolves the recipient\'s
                        locale and selects the matching template.

  Email dispatch        POST /projects/:id/invoices/:id/submit triggers
  (SendGrid)            an email to approver --- email template selected
                        by approver\'s preferred_language, not the
                        submitter\'s.

  SMS dispatch (Twilio) Same locale resolution as email --- recipient\'s
                        language, not sender\'s.

  PDF generation        PDF language is set by the requesting user\'s
  (invoices, reports)   locale --- owner generates a Spanish PDF for a
                        Spanish-speaking client.

  Audit log entries     Always in English --- audit logs are internal
                        records for compliance, never translated.

  User-entered data     Returned as stored --- the API never translates
                        user content. Only system-generated text is
                        localized.
  -----------------------------------------------------------------------

**16.3 Language Preference Endpoints**

  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  **Method**   **Endpoint**            **Auth**   **Description**
  ------------ ----------------------- ---------- ------------------------------------
  PUT          /users/me/language      JWT        Update current user\'s
                                                  preferred_language --- body: {
                                                  preferred_language: \'es\' }.
                                                  Immediately affects all subsequent
                                                  notifications and API responses.

  PUT          /tenant/language        JWT        Update tenant default_language and
                                                  supported_languages array. Owner
                                                  only. Affects language options shown
                                                  to all new team members.

  GET          /locales                None       Returns list of supported language
                                                  codes with display names --- used to
                                                  populate language selector UI. No
                                                  auth required.

  GET          /locales/:code/status   JWT        Returns translation completeness
                                                  status for a given locale --- what
                                                  percentage of strings are
                                                  translated. Used in Settings \>
                                                  Language to show translation
                                                  coverage.
  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**16.4 Accept-Language Header Standard**

-   All API clients (web app, mobile app) MUST include Accept-Language
    header on every request

-   Format: Accept-Language: es or Accept-Language: pt-BR --- standard
    IETF BCP 47 language tag

-   JWT token includes preferred_language claim --- refreshed when user
    updates language preference

-   Server ignores Accept-Language if preferred_language is set in JWT
    --- JWT always wins

-   For unauthenticated endpoints (signup, login, forgot-password), only
    Accept-Language header is used for response locale
